# Windows batch files must use CRLF line endings. cmd.exe mis-parses
# parenthesised blocks and goto labels when the file is LF-only, which is easy
# to introduce by accident on Linux or macOS. Forcing CRLF here means the files
# are correct no matter what core.autocrlf is set to on the machine that
# checks them out.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
